WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.040 --> 00:00:05.840
It’s crazy when you think about all of
the different kinds of foods we eat.

00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:09.760
We just swallow and hope
it all works out for the best.

00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:11.280
Well, as it turns out,

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:15.680
there are better ways to think about keeping
our bodies humming healthfully along.

00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:18.080
Welcome to the
Nutrition Facts Podcast,

00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:20.720
I’m your host,
Dr. Michael Greger.

00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:24.720
If you look inside your mouth
and you find lacy white patches,

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:26.320
sometimes with redness or sores,

00:00:26.320 --> 00:00:29.440
on the inside of the
cheeks, tongue, or gums,

00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:34.240
you may have the inflammatory
condition oral lichen planus.

00:00:34.240 --> 00:00:36.800
Here is one way to treat it.

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:39.120
There's an inflammatory
autoimmune condition

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:40.960
known as oral lichen planus,

00:00:40.960 --> 00:00:45.333
in which our immune system starts
attacking the lining of our mouth.

00:00:45.333 --> 00:00:47.280
This is what it looks like.
It's actually not that rare,

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:49.200
it strikes up to five percent
of the population,

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:50.160
particularly women,

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:54.000
and about one percent of cases
can turn into cancer.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:55.120
There's no cure,

00:00:55.120 --> 00:00:56.960
there's just
symptomatic treatments:

00:00:56.960 --> 00:01:01.760
steroids, immunosuppressants,
and total glucosides of peony.

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:03.520
Like, peony peony?

00:01:03.520 --> 00:01:07.600
Yes, medicinal properties in the
root of the common garden peony.

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:08.640
That's neat.

00:01:08.640 --> 00:01:12.000
But are there any edible plants
that may help?

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:14.320
There's a plant called purslane,

00:01:14.320 --> 00:01:16.800
one of the most common weeds
in the worldâ€”

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:19.120
you can see it growing out
of the cracks in the sidewalk

00:01:19.120 --> 00:01:21.280
everywhere you look,
once you start looking.

00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:23.840
Its healing properties
were thought to be so reliable

00:01:23.840 --> 00:01:26.000
that Roman savant
Pliny the Elder

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:31.360
advised wearing the plant
as an amulet to expel all evil.

00:01:31.360 --> 00:01:32.480
I don't know about that.

00:01:32.480 --> 00:01:34.240
What about just eating it?

00:01:34.240 --> 00:01:36.320
A randomized, double-blind,
placebo-controlled trial

00:01:36.320 --> 00:01:38.960
found that 83 percent
of those in the purslane group

00:01:38.960 --> 00:01:42.480
experienced partial or complete
clinical improvement,

00:01:42.480 --> 00:01:44.560
compared to 83 percent
in the placebo group

00:01:44.560 --> 00:01:47.760
who either didn't respond
or got worse.

00:01:47.760 --> 00:01:51.120
So, this simple weed appears
to be clinically effective

00:01:51.120 --> 00:01:52.960
in the treatment
of oral lichen planus,

00:01:52.960 --> 00:01:54.800
with no side effects.

00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:56.800
In a comparison
to the efficacy and safety

00:01:56.800 --> 00:01:58.000
of nine different treatments,

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:00.320
including steroids
and immunosuppressants,

00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:03.200
purslane appeared to not only
be the safest,

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:05.600
but the most effective
treatment available,

00:02:05.600 --> 00:02:07.280
with only good side-effects:

00:02:07.280 --> 00:02:10.640
lowering triglycerides
and decreasing inflammation.

00:02:10.640 --> 00:02:12.480
You can overdo it, though.

00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:14.480
Purslane is a high oxalate green,

00:02:14.480 --> 00:02:16.960
with nearly half as much
oxalates as spinach.

00:02:16.960 --> 00:02:19.120
So, even if you don't
tend to get kidney stones,

00:02:19.120 --> 00:02:23.200
you don't want to eat four pounds
(2 kg) of purslane at a time.

00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:25.040
I know it's delicious,

00:02:25.040 --> 00:02:27.200
but as little as a pound and a half
(0.70 kg) at a time,

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:29.440
or even two pounds (0.90 kg)
spread out over two meals

00:02:29.440 --> 00:02:32.880
could potentially overload
the kidney and cause damage.

00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:35.680
Purslane can even fight
lichen planus topically.

00:02:35.680 --> 00:02:39.200
A purslane gel appeared to work
as well as topical steroids,

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:40.800
the gold standard treatment.

00:02:40.800 --> 00:02:45.200
The researchers concluded that
purslane is a "magical" herb:

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:46.800
beneficial,
lacking side effects,

00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:49.120
and therefore can be
a safer alternative drug

00:02:49.120 --> 00:02:51.200
in oral lichen planus treatment.

00:02:51.200 --> 00:02:53.120
But by alternative "drug"

00:02:53.120 --> 00:02:58.640
they're just talking about a weed
that grows for free all over.

00:02:58.640 --> 00:02:59.440
In our next story,

00:02:59.440 --> 00:03:03.200
we look at additional ways
to treat lichen planus.

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:07.120
Lichen planus is a chronic
autoimmune disease,

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:10.640
typically of our moist membranes,
such as the inside of our mouth,

00:03:10.640 --> 00:03:13.575
but can also affect other body surfaces.

00:03:13.650 --> 00:03:15.920
Current treatments are not curative

00:03:15.920 --> 00:03:19.680
but rather palliative,
aimed at relieving pain.

00:03:19.680 --> 00:03:23.360
We’ve tried steroids, antibiotics,
chemotherapy, and surgery,

00:03:23.360 --> 00:03:26.400
and none appear to be
particularly effective.

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:28.800
So, even for palliative pain relief,

00:03:28.800 --> 00:03:30.400
we don’t have great options;

00:03:30.400 --> 00:03:34.157
that’s why case reports
like this are so exciting.

00:03:34.240 --> 00:03:38.640
After drinking 2 ounces
of aloe vera juice a day

00:03:38.640 --> 00:03:42.034
and applying aloe topically as well.

00:03:42.160 --> 00:03:48.400
But, is ingested oral aloe
vera a potion or poison?

00:03:48.400 --> 00:03:50.640
Internal use of aloe may cause

00:03:50.640 --> 00:03:53.120
acute hepatitis—liver inflammation,

00:03:53.120 --> 00:03:54.960
as well as electrolyte imbalances,

00:03:54.960 --> 00:03:59.760
and you should definitely not inject aloe.

00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:03.680
But oral use is also not
recommended either.

00:04:03.680 --> 00:04:05.760
This is primarily because of case reports

00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:07.680
of aloe-induced hepatitis.

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:11.200
Aloe is, ironically, presented
as a detoxifying product

00:04:11.200 --> 00:04:14.339
but can actually end
up causing liver damage.

00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:18.160
How do we know it was the aloe, though?

00:04:18.160 --> 00:04:21.653
The assessment of suspected
herbal-induced liver injury

00:04:21.653 --> 00:04:23.840
is challenging, because
there’s hundreds of things

00:04:23.840 --> 00:04:25.840
out there that can damage your liver.

00:04:25.840 --> 00:04:27.280
Here’s the kind of checklist

00:04:27.280 --> 00:04:29.360
you have to go through as a doctor

00:04:29.360 --> 00:04:33.360
to rule out other causes before
you blame it on the plant.

00:04:33.360 --> 00:04:35.680
Do you have some kind of viral hepatitis,

00:04:35.680 --> 00:04:37.280
or other kind of liver infection,

00:04:37.280 --> 00:04:39.760
or it could be various drugs
or toxins and diseases.

00:04:39.760 --> 00:04:42.000
So, maybe it was one
of these other things,

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:43.600
and it was just a coincidence

00:04:43.600 --> 00:04:46.720
that the problem started
after drinking aloe.

00:04:46.720 --> 00:04:48.720
The gold standard, in terms of trying

00:04:48.720 --> 00:04:52.800
to prove cause-and-effect, is
a positive re-exposure test—

00:04:52.800 --> 00:04:55.920
that’s how you can diagnose
drug-induced liver injury.

00:04:55.920 --> 00:04:58.560
Liver inflammation disappears
when you remove the drug,

00:04:58.560 --> 00:05:02.240
and then reappears when
you add the drug back,

00:05:02.240 --> 00:05:04.560
which is rarely done,
for obvious reasons.

00:05:04.560 --> 00:05:05.600
Well, has there ever been

00:05:05.600 --> 00:05:09.520
a re-challenge case published for aloe?

00:05:09.520 --> 00:05:11.120
Yes.

00:05:11.120 --> 00:05:14.320
Aloe-induced toxic
hepatitis that shot up again

00:05:14.320 --> 00:05:18.960
after stopping then
restarting aloe ingestion.

00:05:18.960 --> 00:05:22.320
Aloe consumption has also been
linked to thyroid dysfunction.

00:05:22.320 --> 00:05:24.480
A woman with lichen
planus started swallowing

00:05:24.480 --> 00:05:26.960
2 teaspoons of aloe vera juice a day.

00:05:26.960 --> 00:05:30.160
She started feeling unjustifiably tired.

00:05:30.160 --> 00:05:32.720
Labwork showed her
thyroid function was low,

00:05:32.720 --> 00:05:35.840
but she perked right back
up after stopping the aloe,

00:05:35.840 --> 00:05:39.360
and her thyroid function
returned to normal.

00:05:39.360 --> 00:05:41.280
What if, instead of swallowing, though,

00:05:41.280 --> 00:05:43.200
she just swished the
aloe around in her mouth

00:05:43.200 --> 00:05:44.640
to try to help the lichen planus

00:05:44.640 --> 00:05:46.720
and then spit it out?

00:05:46.720 --> 00:05:47.840
We didn’t know...

00:05:47.840 --> 00:05:51.280
until it was put to the test.

00:05:51.280 --> 00:05:54.160
A randomized, double-blind,
placebo-controlled trial:

00:05:54.160 --> 00:05:57.360
54 patients randomized to
a topical aloe vera gel

00:05:57.360 --> 00:06:00.400
or placebo gel for 8 weeks.

00:06:00.400 --> 00:06:02.640
81% in the aloe group got better

00:06:02.640 --> 00:06:06.400
compared to just 4% in the placebo group.

00:06:06.400 --> 00:06:08.400
Furthermore, two patients
treated with aloe

00:06:08.400 --> 00:06:11.760
had a complete clinical remission.

00:06:11.760 --> 00:06:12.960
That’s rare.

00:06:12.960 --> 00:06:14.800
It’s considered a chronic condition;

00:06:14.800 --> 00:06:16.240
yet, a few weeks applying aloe,

00:06:16.240 --> 00:06:20.800
and the nasty erosive
lesions disappeared.

00:06:20.800 --> 00:06:24.560
How about compared to a
steroid ointment, though?

00:06:24.560 --> 00:06:28.480
Topical aloe vera gel was superior—

00:06:28.480 --> 00:06:30.640
more effective than the steroids,

00:06:30.640 --> 00:06:33.840
a significant difference
appearing within 2 weeks.

00:06:33.840 --> 00:06:35.520
So, although corticosteroids are

00:06:35.520 --> 00:06:37.040
still considered the gold standard,

00:06:37.040 --> 00:06:39.520
aloe vera shows promising results,

00:06:39.520 --> 00:06:41.600
especially with no adverse effects,

00:06:41.600 --> 00:06:44.480
when applied topically,
compared to various adverse

00:06:44.480 --> 00:06:47.600
side effects of the corticosteroids.

00:06:47.600 --> 00:06:50.480
That’s for oral lichen planus, though.

00:06:50.480 --> 00:06:53.200
What about the efficacy of aloe vera gel

00:06:53.200 --> 00:06:56.160
in the treatment of lichen
planus of the genitals?

00:06:56.160 --> 00:06:58.720
Lichen planus of the
vulva is quite common,

00:06:58.720 --> 00:07:02.080
affecting 1-2% of the population,

00:07:02.080 --> 00:07:05.120
and it may be even harder to treat.

00:07:05.120 --> 00:07:07.200
There are flares and partial remission

00:07:07.200 --> 00:07:09.680
but no tendency for complete remission.

00:07:09.680 --> 00:07:13.600
And, indeed, that’s what they
saw in the placebo group.

00:07:13.600 --> 00:07:17.040
One woman had a good response,
but most had little or no response,

00:07:17.040 --> 00:07:19.760
but applying aloe vera gel instead,

00:07:19.760 --> 00:07:22.160
and 9 out of 10 responded,

00:07:22.160 --> 00:07:26.160
and one woman had a
complete clinical remission.

00:07:26.160 --> 00:07:31.600
They conclude that aloe vera gel
is a safe and effective treatment.

